course: dictionary
lesson: 1553
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which one fits. «She won the championship after three years of training.» The word championship here means the title of being the best, not a competition.
explain: A championship is a competition to find the best player or team in a sport or game. Schools can have their own championships too, such as a chess or spelling championship. Read the words around the word to see which meaning the writer means.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The world championship starts on Monday» works with the meaning competition. In formal writing, championship can also mean strong support for a cause, as in «his championship of animal rights».
fact: A championship is a competition to find the best player or team in a sport or game.
fact: Championship can also mean the title or position of being the champion, as in «She won the championship.»
fact: «The Lionesses won the European Championship in 2022 and again in 2025.» The Lionesses are England's women's football team.
fact: The game of conkers has a world championship held every year in England.
fact: In formal writing, championship can mean strong support for a cause.
exercise: «She won the championship after three years of training.» What does championship mean here? | *The title of being the best | A small school trip | A sort of sports shoe | Wet grass on a pitch
exercise: Sam says championship means a sad, quiet mood. What is the mistake? | Sam is right, it means a sad mood | *It is a competition or title, not a feeling | It means a loud noise | It is a kind of animal
exercise: «The game of conkers has a world championship held every year in England.» Find and copy one word that means a big competition to find the best. | *championship | every | conkers | England
test: «England's women's football team won the European Championship in 2022.» What is the European Championship? | A shop that sells football shirts | A school sports day | *A big competition to find the best team in Europe | A kind of football boot
test: What does «his championship of animal rights» mean? | A pet shop | A competition for animals | He is a champion at swimming | *Strong support for a cause
exam: Which word means a competition to find the best player or team? | *championship | title | cause | conkers
